flow "Chandy-Lamport global snapshot"
summary "Captures a consistent global state across processes without pausing execution by sending markers on FIFO channels and logging in-flight messages."
tags snapshots distributed-algorithms consistency
level advanced
source "https://lamport.azurewebsites.net/pubs/chandy.pdf"
related distributed-systems/lamport-clocks

node p1 "Process P1 ($100)" service tone=primary
node p2 "Process P2 ($100)" service
node snap "Snapshot Store" db
edge p1 > p2
edge p1 > snap dashed
edge p2 > snap dashed
array rec "Snapshot (total must be $200)" keys=p1,p2,chan-12 = - - empty

scenario clean-snap "Consistent snapshot with no in-flight messages"
  step start "P2 initiates snapshot and sends Marker"
    "Two processes hold `$200` total (`$100` each). To snapshot without stopping the world, P2 records its local state (`$100`), starts logging incoming messages, and sends a `Marker`."
    state p2 active
    send p2 > snap "save P2=$100"
    label rec#p2 "$100"
    send p2 > p1 "Marker"
  step p1-records "P1 receives Marker, saves state, echoes Marker"
    "On receiving its first `Marker`, P1 records its local state (`$100`) and sends `Marker` back along FIFO channel `P1 -> P2`. No transfer occurred, so the channel log stays empty."
    send p1 > snap "save P1=$100"
    label rec#p1 "$100"
    send p1 > p2 "Marker"
    state p1,p2,snap,rec success
    callout snap "Consistent: $100 + $100 + $0 = $200"

scenario in-flight "In-flight transfer captured in channel state" from=clean-snap/start
  step transfer "P1 had already sent $30 before seeing Marker"
    "Just before P2's `Marker` arrived, P1 transferred `$30` to P2 — dropping P1 to `$70` while `$30` is still **in flight** on channel `P1 -> P2`."
    label p1 "Process P1 ($70)"
    state p1 warning
    send p1 > p2 "$30 (in-flight)"
    callout p1 "Sent $30 before Marker arrived"
  step p1-snap "P1 receives Marker and records $70"
    "P1 now receives P2's `Marker`, records its post-send state `$70`, and puts its own `Marker` onto FIFO channel `P1 -> P2` **behind** the `$30` transfer."
    detail "FIFO ordering is essential here: because the channel cannot reorder messages, P1's `Marker` cannot overtake the `$30` transfer. Every message P1 sent before its local snapshot is guaranteed to reach P2 before P1's `Marker` closes recording."
    send p1 > snap "save P1=$70"
    label rec#p1 "$70"
    send p1 > p2 "Marker (after $30)"
  step log-channel "P2 logs in-flight $30 before P1's Marker closes channel"
    "Because P2 already snapshotted at `$100` and is recording channel `P1 -> P2`, it captures `$30` in `chan-12` before P1's `Marker` closes recording. Total = `$70 + $100 + $30 = $200`!"
    detail "The result is a **consistent global state**: causality is preserved (no message is recorded as received without also being recorded as sent), even though P1 and P2 snapshotted at different wall-clock times. Apache Flink's checkpoint barriers adapt this exact mechanism for streaming recovery."
    label p2 "Process P2 ($130)"
    label rec#chan-12 "$30"
    state rec#chan-12 active with
    send p2 > snap "chan-12=$30"
    state p1,p2,snap,rec success
    callout snap "FIFO marker preserved the $30 in flight!"
